{"name":"Embarcadero","hex":"#5d4643","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"embarcadero","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A quay; a wharf.","1 2 3 “‖embarcaˈdero” listed in the Oxford English Dictionary [2 Ed.; 1989]"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/embarcadero"}],"entries":[{"title":"Embarcadero (San Diego)","blocks":[{"text":"The Embarcadero in San Diego, California, is the area along the San Diego harbor on the east side of San Diego Bay. \"Embarcadero\" is a Spanish word meaning \"boarding place\". The Embarcadero sits on property administered by the Port of San Diego, in the Columbia district of downtown San Diego."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Embarcadero_(San_Diego)"},{"title":"Embarcadero (San Francisco)","blocks":[{"text":"The Embarcadero is the eastern waterfront of Port of San Francisco and a major roadway in San Francisco, California, United States. It was constructed on reclaimed land along a three mile long engineered seawall, from which piers extend into the bay. It derives its name from the Spanish verb embarcar, meaning \"to embark\"; embarcadero itself means \"the place to embark.\" The Central Embarcadero Piers Historic District was added to the National Register of Historic Places on November 20, 2002."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/The_Embarcadero%2C_San_Francisco.jpg/330px-The_Embarcadero%2C_San_Francisco.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Embarcadero_(San_Francisco)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/North_Embarcadero.jpg/500px-North_Embarcadero.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/North_Embarcadero.jpg/1280px-North_Embarcadero.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/North_Embarcadero.jpg/500px-North_Embarcadero.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"North Embarcadero in 2006","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANorth_Embarcadero.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Edward_J._Livernash_Addressing_Open-Air_Meeting%2C_1902.jpg/500px-Edward_J._Livernash_Addressing_Open-Air_Meeting%2C_1902.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Edward_J._Livernash_Addressing_Open-Air_Meeting%2C_1902.jpg/1280px-Edward_J._Livernash_Addressing_Open-Air_Meeting%2C_1902.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Edward_J._Livernash_Addressing_Open-Air_Meeting%2C_1902.jpg/500px-Edward_J._Livernash_Addressing_Open-Air_Meeting%2C_1902.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Congressional candidate Edward J. Livernash gives a speech at the Pacific Mail Docks on the corner of 1st and Brannan Streets, October 17, 1902","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEdward_J._Livernash_Addressing_Open-Air_Meeting%2C_1902.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/View_of_Yerba_Buena_Island%2C_Bay_Bridge.jpg/500px-View_of_Yerba_Buena_Island%2C_Bay_Bridge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/View_of_Yerba_Buena_Island%2C_Bay_Bridge.jpg/1280px-View_of_Yerba_Buena_Island%2C_Bay_Bridge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/View_of_Yerba_Buena_Island%2C_Bay_Bridge.jpg/500px-View_of_Yerba_Buena_Island%2C_Bay_Bridge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnai